{
  "_readme": [
    "OFFICIAL NJ EQUALIZATION RATIOS  \u00b7  TAX YEAR 2026  \u00b7  SOUTH JERSEY",
    "",
    "Source: NJ Division of Taxation, 'Certification of Average Ratios and Common",
    "Level Ranges for Use in the Tax Year 2026', Chapter 123 Laws of 1973.",
    "Original certification October 1, 2025, as amended by the NJ Tax Court",
    "January 30, 2026. Director Marita R. Sciarrotta.",
    "https://www.nj.gov/treasury/taxation/pdf/lpt/chap123/2026CH123.pdf",
    "",
    "WHAT THESE DO:",
    "  market value = assessed value / (ratio / 100)",
    "  A $200,000 assessment in a town at 58.00 implies a $344,828 home.",
    "  The same assessment in a town at 94.03 implies a $212,700 home.",
    "",
    "  'lower' and 'upper' are the Chapter 123 common level range. If an",
    "  assessment exceeds the upper limit applied to true market value, the county",
    "  board is directed to reduce it. That is the whole basis of an appeal, and",
    "  the page uses these published limits rather than computing its own.",
    "",
    "COVERAGE: all 168 municipalities in the seven South Jersey counties.",
    "  Atlantic 23, Burlington 40, Camden 36, Cape May 16, Cumberland 14,",
    "  Gloucester 24, Salem 15.",
    "",
    "KEY FORMAT: 'MUNICIPALITY (COUNTY)'. Every key is county qualified on",
    "  purpose. WASHINGTON TWP and GREENWICH TWP each exist in more than one",
    "  South Jersey county with different ratios, so a bare town name would be",
    "  ambiguous. Names match MUN_NAME as returned by the state parcel service.",
    "",
    "ADDING MORE COUNTIES:",
    "  Pull the same PDF for the year you want, find the county block, and add",
    "  entries in this format. Ocean, Mercer, Monmouth and the north are all in",
    "  the same document.",
    "",
    "UPDATING EACH YEAR:",
    "  The state certifies in October for the following tax year, and the Tax",
    "  Court may amend it in January. Add the new year alongside the old one:",
    "    'WINSLOW TWP (CAMDEN)': { '2026': {...}, '2027': {...} }",
    "  The page automatically uses the most recent year present.",
    "",
    "VERIFICATION: every row was checked against the state's own arithmetic,",
    "  lower = ratio x 0.85 and upper = ratio x 1.15. All 168 matched exactly.",
    "  Stored upper values mirror the printed certification table. For Chapter 123",
    "  use, any upper ratio above 100% is legally treated as 100%; the browser",
    "  applies that cap when it reads the certified corridor."
  ],
